{"duration_api_ms":655452,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"82312e0d-84f4-418f-aa4b-0abc53f02c04","total_cost_usd":29.43065,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484187,"cache_read_input_tokens":3353487,"output_tokens":3780,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":403},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":484187,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1370,"cache_read_input_tokens":481385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2802},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":220,"outputTokens":53730,"thinkingTokens":13117,"cacheReadInputTokens":42031160,"cacheCreationInputTokens":707072,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":29.43065,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The fingerprint is in place and nothing else changed.\n\n## What I did\n\nFilled `ANTIFRAUD_CERT_SHA256` with the fingerprint you supplied, as a single entry in uppercase hex without colons — the format the doc comment already specified. `isSignedBy` normalises with `e.replace(\":\", \"\").equalsIgnoreCase(actual)`, so this matches the digest it builds (uppercase, `%02X`, no separators); colons would also have worked. The comment now records the source: the v2 signing certificate of the official release APKs (tags 6.4.5-fix, 6.3.5, 6.2.5), as printed by `apksigner verify --print-certs`.\n\nI checked the transcription with a script rather than by eye: the 32 bytes in the file are identical to your value with colons stripped.\n\nFail-closed behaviour is untouched — a package that is missing, not visible, has multiple signers, or whose certificate does not match still gets nothing sent and shows the toast. The empty-array guard stays as a safety net.\n\n## Diff\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/android/app/src/main/java/com/example/piliplus/AndroidHelper.java b/android/app/src/main/java/com/example/piliplus/AndroidHelper.java\n@@\n      * (https://github.com/freedom-introvert/biliSendCommAntifraud). The full\n      * cookie string is only handed to a package signed with one of these.\n      * <p>\n-     * Empty: no authoritative fingerprint is recorded in this repository, so\n-     * the check fails closed and nothing is sent. To enable the feature, add\n-     * the fingerprint printed by\n-     * {@code apksigner verify --print-certs <official release apk>}\n-     * (\"Signer #1 certificate SHA-256 digest\"), without colons.\n+     * Taken from the v2 signing certificate of the official release APKs\n+     * (tags 6.4.5-fix, 6.3.5 and 6.2.5 all carry this one), as printed by\n+     * {@code apksigner verify --print-certs <apk>} (\"Signer #1 certificate\n+     * SHA-256 digest\"). A package signed by anything else gets nothing.\n      */\n-    private static final String[] ANTIFRAUD_CERT_SHA256 = {};\n+    private static final String[] ANTIFRAUD_CERT_SHA256 = {\n+            \"0225A7553765722353B0A27980F779A4ECF8302AFB27911E3D42AACBECAA31BF\",\n+    };\n```\n\n(The rest of the `AndroidHelper.java` hunk shown by `git diff` is the pass-3 D4 change from the previous turn, unchanged here.)\n\nThe Java cannot be compiled in this environment. What I verified by reading: the constant is a `String[]` initialiser with a valid Java string literal and trailing comma, it stays inside the same class body, and the only reference to it is the `isSignedBy(ANTIFRAUD_PACKAGE, ANTIFRAUD_CERT_SHA256)` call, whose parameter is `@NonNull String[]`.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (preceded by dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source local_env.sh && cd C:/Users/Z14/Documents/Coding/Piliplus && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 102\n  passed: 102\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~298000 (analyze ~280s, test ~18s)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` exits 0 with the same 36 info-level issues as before (no errors, no warnings, none in the files this pass touched), and all 102 tests pass. Neither run exercises the Java, so they only confirm the Dart side is unaffected.","ttft_ms":13112,"type":"result","duration_ms":293699,"uuid":"68a0af4c-d5f2-4e6e-968b-5b8376b41bd4","ttft_stream_ms":11386,"time_to_request_ms":628,"first_content_frame_ms":11386,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
